problem:
Problem description
- There is a finite set $$I$$ of children, indexed by $$i \in I$$.
- Each child $$i \in I$$ has an associated selection cost $$w_i$$.
- The family must choose a subset $$S \subseteq I$$ of children for the trip.
- The number of selected children is limited by a maximum capacity $$K$$.
- The family also requires that the selected group contain at least a minimum number $$L$$ of children.
- There is a designated subset $$I^{\mathrm{fix}} \subseteq I$$ of mandatory children that must always be included.
- There is a set of ordered incompatibility rules $$\mathcal{F} \subseteq I \times I$$, where selecting a child in the first position makes the child in the second position unavailable.
- There is a set of ordered prerequisite rules $$\mathcal{R} \subseteq I \times I$$, where selecting a child in the first position requires selecting the child in the second position as well.
- The planning goal is to select a feasible subset of children with minimum total selection cost.

- The selected group must not exceed the trip capacity $$K$$.
- The selected group must contain at least $$L$$ children.
- Every child in $$I^{\mathrm{fix}}$$ must be selected.
- Every incompatibility rule in $$\mathcal{F}$$ must be respected.
- Every prerequisite rule in $$\mathcal{R}$$ must be respected.
- The objective is to minimize the sum of the costs of all selected children.

- A solution is represented by:
  - A binary decision variable $$x_i \in \{0,1\}$$ for each $$i \in I$$, where $$x_i = 1$$ means child $$i$$ is selected and $$x_i = 0$$ means child $$i$$ is not selected.
  - The selected set $$S = \{\, i \in I \mid x_i = 1 \,\}$$.
  - The resulting total cost of the chosen subset.

Input Format
{
  "children_set": "finite set $$I$$ of children",
  "children_count": "number of children $$n = |I|$$",
  "selection_costs": {
    "type": "vector of length $$n$$",
    "meaning": "$$w_i$$ is the cost of selecting child $$i$$ for each $$i \\in I$$"
  },
  "capacity_limit": {
    "type": "scalar",
    "meaning": "maximum number of children that may be selected, denoted by $$K$$"
  },
  "minimum_selected": {
    "type": "scalar",
    "meaning": "minimum number of children that must be selected, denoted by $$L$$"
  },
  "mandatory_children": {
    "type": "subset of $$I$$",
    "meaning": "$$I^{\\mathrm{fix}}$$, the set of children that must be selected"
  },
  "forbidden_pairs": {
    "type": "list of ordered pairs",
    "meaning": "each pair $$(i,j) \\in \\mathcal{F}$$ means that if $$i$$ is selected, then $$j$$ cannot be selected"
  },
  "prerequisite_pairs": {
    "type": "list of ordered pairs",
    "meaning": "each pair $$(i,j) \\in \\mathcal{R}$$ means that if $$i$$ is selected, then $$j$$ must also be selected"
  },
  "objective": {
    "type": "minimization",
    "meaning": "minimize the total cost of the selected children"
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "selected_children": {
    "type": "list",
    "meaning": "the identifiers of all selected children in the optimal feasible solution"
  },
  "selection_vector": {
    "type": "binary vector",
    "shape": "$$n$$",
    "meaning": "$$x_i = 1$$ if child $$i$$ is selected and $$x_i = 0$$ otherwise"
  },
  "total_cost": {
    "type": "scalar",
    "meaning": "the minimized sum of the selected children’s costs"
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "children_set": ["Alice", "Bob", "Charlie", "Diana", "Ella"],
  "selection_costs": {
    "Alice": 1000,
    "Bob": 900,
    "Charlie": 600,
    "Diana": 500,
    "Ella": 700
  },
  "capacity_limit": 3,
  "minimum_selected": 2,
  "mandatory_children": ["Bob"],
  "forbidden_pairs": [
    ["Alice", "Diana"],
    ["Bob", "Charlie"]
  ],
  "prerequisite_pairs": [
    ["Charlie", "Diana"],
    ["Diana", "Ella"]
  ]
}
